# Debugging Email Watcher

The user reports that the system is not processing requests from emails. I need to verify the connection to Exchange and the filtering logic.

## Proposed Changes

### [Component] Email Watcher Debugging

#### [NEW] [debug_exchange.py](file:///c:/projects/it-inventory/it-inventory/inventory_app/debug_exchange.py)
Create a standalone script to test the Exchange connection and list recent emails without creating database entries, providing verbose output.

#### [MODIFY] [email_watcher.py](file:///c:/projects/it-inventory/it-inventory/inventory_app/email_watcher.py)
Improve logging to show exactly why an email was skipped (e.g., if it didn't match keywords or sender filter).

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
1. Run `python debug_exchange.py` to see if it can connect to the configured Exchange account.
2. Check the output for any "Skipped" messages and the reasons.

### Manual Verification
1. Ask the user to send a test email from the whitelisted sender and check the logs.
2. If Docker is preferred, I will help the user start Docker Desktop or troubleshoot the Docker connection.
